# Uniform by-reference capture (F3 / B2 parity guard). A closure `f` that captures a by-reference
# local (`x`, a cell) is invoked inside a `spawn` task via the call form `spawn f()`. Whichever way
# the task's copy of `f` and its cell are reconstructed, the print is
# post-join, so it prints `7` exactly.
#
# M3.4: the task gets `f` itself, with the parent's captured cell (by handle). This read-only case
# prints `7`; the mutation forms (a closure mutating a captured cell's inner heap value, or reading a
# cell the owner writes after spawn) are in `capture_spawn_closure_mutates_shared.chz` /
# `capture_spawn_closure_owner_write_shared.chz`.
fn main():
    x := 7
    ch := Channel[int]()
    f := fn(): ch.send(x)
    parallel:
        spawn f()
    print(ch.recv())            # 7

main()
